     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt;color:#000000\">  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Dear all,</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">I have prepared a coloured graph (attached) for publication in a journal which I now have to change into black and white </span><span style=\"font-family:Wingdings\" lang=\"EN-GB\"><span>:-(</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> (attached). Otherwise, I’d have to pay ca. 1000 $ for 3 graphs, seriously.</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">I have attached a reproducible R script. It first presents the graph in colour and then in black and white which shows the dilemma.</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Ideally, I would like to have the “line” AND the “fill” in the legend, not only the “line”. “Fill” only would be good too. Of course I could use different line\n types but for a crossbar it would look a bit stupid. The other alternative would be to use a white line for the second group but really, that would not produce a great legend as well.</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">If anybody could help me include the fill in the legend or has a good alternative I would be very grateful.</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Best wishes,</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Martin</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">p.s.: The session info is:</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"># R version 2.12.0 (2010-10-15)</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"># Platform: i386-pc-mingw32/i386 (32-bit)</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"># locale:</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"># [1] LC_COLLATE=German_Austria.1252<span>  </span>LC_CTYPE=German_Austria.1252<span>    </span>LC_MONETARY=German_Austria.1252 LC_NUMERIC=C<span>                    </span>LC_TIME=German_Austria.1252<span>    </span></span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"># attached base packages:</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"># [1]\n grid<span>      </span>stats<span>     </span>graphics<span>  </span>grDevices utils<span>     </span>datasets<span>  </span>methods<span>   </span>base<span>     </span></span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"># other attached packages:</span></p>  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"># [1] ggplot2_0.8.8 digest_0.4.2<span>  </span>reshape_0.8.3 plyr_1.2.1<span>    </span>proto_0.3-8<span>  <br></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"><span><br></span></span></p>  <div> </div><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><strong>Martin H.\n Kärcher</strong></font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><strong></strong>Laboratory of Apiculture &amp; Social Insects</font></p> <p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Department of Biology &amp; Environmental Science</span></p> <p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\">School</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> of Life Sciences</span></p> <p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\">John</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> Maynard Smith  Building</span></p> <p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\">University</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> of Sussex</span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Brighton</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> BN1 9QG, UK</span><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">landline (Austria): <a href=\"tel:+43%20316%20382448\" value=\"+43316382448\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+43 316 382448</a></font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">mobile (Austria): <a href=\"tel:+43%20650%203824481\" value=\"+436503824481\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+43 650 3824481</a></font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">landline (England): +44 127 367 8103<br></font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.sussex.ac.uk/biology/profile220918.html\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.sussex.ac.uk/biology/profile220918.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792381228197000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3o4vvMLiJPBH_hogglG_Vu\"><font style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">http://www.sussex.ac.uk/biology/profile220918.html</font></a></p><div><br></div> </div><br></div>"
