   "subject": "RE: fill in legend of black & white crossbar plot",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div lang=\"ES-TRAD\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Hi Martin,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">As a workaround, you can just add a layer which takes fill as a valid aesthetic (I guess, after looking at the online documentation, that’s the reason why if you only include geom_crossbar the fill doesn’t appear in the legend [e.g. hollow bar …]); in the code bellow I just added geom_smooth() (you only receive a warning saying you have only one x value and nothing to draw). <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Hope this helps, and congratulations,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">fernando<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">ggplot(df, aes(fill = group, colour = group, y = resp, x = trt)) +<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                geom_crossbar(limits,  width = 0.7, position = position_dodge(width = 0.8), size = 0.8) +<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                geom_smooth() +<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                scale_fill_manual(values = alpha(c(&quot;white&quot;, &quot;black&quot;), 0.3), name = &quot;&quot;) +<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                scale_colour_manual(values = c(&quot;black&quot;, &quot;black&quot;), name = &quot;&quot;) +<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                scale_y_continuous(breaks = seq(36, 50, 2), name = &quot;&quot;) +<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                scale_x_discrete(name = &quot;&quot;) +<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                opts(legend.position = c(0.764, 0.833),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                               legend.background = theme_rect(colour = 0),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                               legend.text = theme_text(face = &quot;italic&quot;, size = 20),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                               legend.title = theme_blank()) +<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                opts(axis.text.x = theme_text(size = 20, vjust = 1),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                               axis.text.y = theme_text(size = 20, hjust = 1)) +<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                opts(axis.title.x = theme_text(size = 27, hjust = 0.561, vjust = 0.3),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                               axis.title.y = theme_text(size = 27, angle = 90, vjust = 0.685, hjust = 0.78)) +<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">                opts(plot.margin = unit (c(1.1, 1, 1.28, 1.23), &quot;lines&quot;))<u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"ES-TRAD\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a name=\"m_5065894408708763049__MailEndCompose\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><div><div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm 0cm 0cm\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"ES\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">De:</span></b><span lang=\"ES\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>] <b>En nombre de </b>Martin Kärcher<br><b>Enviado el:</b> jueves, 25 de noviembre de 2010 18:57<br><b>Para:</b> ggplot2<br><b>Asunto:</b> fill in legend of black &amp; white crossbar plot<u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\">Dear all,</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\">I have prepared a coloured graph (attached) for publication in a journal which I now have to change into black and white </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family:Wingdings;color:black\">:-(</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"> (attached). Otherwise, I’d have to pay ca. 1000 $ for 3 graphs, seriously.</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\">I have attached a reproducible R script. It first presents the graph in colour and then in black and white which shows the dilemma.</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\">Ideally, I would like to have the “line” AND the “fill” in the legend, not only the “line”. “Fill” only would be good too. Of course I could use different line types but for a crossbar it would look a bit stupid. The other alternative would be to use a white line for the second group but really, that would not produce a great legend as well.</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\">If anybody could help me include the fill in the legend or has a good alternative I would be very grateful.</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\">Best wishes,</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\">Martin</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\">p.s.: The session info is:</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"># R version 2.12.0 (2010-10-15)</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"># Platform: i386-pc-mingw32/i386 (32-bit)</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"># locale:</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"># [1] LC_COLLATE=German_Austria.1252  LC_CTYPE=German_Austria.1252    LC_MONETARY=German_Austria.1252 LC_NUMERIC=C                    LC_TIME=German_Austria.1252    </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"># attached base packages:</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"># [1] grid      stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"># other attached packages:</span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:black\"># [1] ggplot2_0.8.8 digest_0.4.2  reshape_0.8.3 plyr_1.2.1    proto_0.3-8  </span><span style=