     "<div lang=\"ES-TRAD\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>Please provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"http://gist.github.com/270442\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://gist.github.com/270442&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792381228204000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2crcok0P-xG2xCTz4Zfc0z\">http://gist.github.com/270442</a><br> <br>To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>More options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792381228204000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Y6nzNsK7rp-LmJ2KCGxu7\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><u></u><u></u></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hyN5qG1-UIMJ",
   "from": "Martin Kärcher",
   "author": "6e0a397d1d4aab5b",
   "date": "2010-11-26T14:48:28Z",
   "subject": "AW: fill in legend of black & white crossbar plot",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\">Hi Fernando,<br><br>Thanks for this excellent solution! I will probably need it for many future graphs. Thanks also for reorganising my code. It is now much clearer. When checking your code I realised that some of my code was actually unnecessary. The code now reads:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\"><br><br>ggplot(df, aes(fill = group, colour = group, y = resp, x = trt)) +<br>    geom_crossbar(limits,  width = 0.7, position = position_dodge(width = 0.8), size = 0.8) +<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\">    geom_smooth(size = 0.8) +<br>    scale_fill_manual(values = alpha(c(&quot;white&quot;, &quot;black&quot;), 0.4), name = &quot;&quot;) +</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\"><br>    scale_colour_manual(values = c(&quot;black&quot;, &quot;black&quot;), name = &quot;&quot;) +<br>    scale_y_continuous(breaks = seq(36, 50, 2), name = &quot;&quot;) +<br>    scale_x_discrete(name\n = &quot;&quot;) +<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\">    opts(legend.position = c(0.764, 0.8334),</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\"><br>        legend.background = theme_rect(colour = 0),<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\">        legend.key = theme_rect(colour = 1, size = 0.6),</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\"><br>        legend.text = theme_text(face = &quot;italic&quot;, size = 20),<br>        legend.title = theme_blank()) +<br>    opts(axis.text.x = theme_text(size = 20, vjust = 1),<br>        axis.text.y = theme_text(size = 20, hjust = 1)) +<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\">    opts(plot.margin = unit (c(1.1, 1, 2, 2), &quot;lines&quot;))<br> <br>    grid.text(&quot;cell type of eggs&quot;, x = unit(0.56, &quot;npc&quot;), y = unit(0.05, &quot;npc&quot;), gp=gpar(fontsize = 27))<br>    grid.text(&quot;time to be replaced [h]&quot;, x = unit(0.04, &quot;npc&quot;), y = unit(0.552, &quot;npc&quot;), rot = 90, gp=gpar(fontsize = 27))<br><br>I have also attached the graph as\n a PDF.<br><br>Do you know if this feature will eventually be included in geom_crossbar? I cannot see a logical reason why &quot;fill&quot; should not be included in the legend of geom_crossbar.<br><br>Best wishes,<br><br>Martin</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\"><br><br><div> </div><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><strong>Martin H. Kärcher</strong></font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><strong></strong>Laboratory of Apiculture &amp; Social Insects</font></p> <p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Department of Biology &amp; Environmental Science</span></p> <p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\">School</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> of Life Sciences</span></p> <p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\">John</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> Maynard Smith  Building</span></p> <p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\">University</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> of Sussex</span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Brighton</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> BN1 9QG, UK</span><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">landline (Austria): <a href=\"tel:+43%20316%20382448\" value=\"+43316382448\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+43 316 382448</a></font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">mobile (Austria): <a href=\"tel:+43%20650%203824481\" value=\"+436503824481\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+43 650 3824481</a></font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">landline (England): +44 127 367 8103<br></font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.sussex.ac.uk/biology/profile220918.html\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.sussex.ac.uk/biology/profile220918.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792381228212000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0XOdZluPOyLU3v7PHN-c2m\"><font style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">http://www.sussex.ac.uk/biology/profile220918.html</font></a></p><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\"><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\"><br><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\"><font face=\"Tahoma\" size=\"2\"><hr size=\"1\"><b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Von:</span></b> fernando &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">fgta...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br><b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">An:</span></b> Martin Kärcher &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">martin_...@yahoo.de</a>&gt;; ggplot2 &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br><b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Gesendet:</span></b> Donnerstag, den 25. November 2010, 18:46:52 Uhr<br><b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Betreff:</span></b> RE: fill in legend of black &amp; white crossbar plot<br></font></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\"><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\"><div style=\"font-family:times new roman,new york,times,serif;font-size:12pt\"><br><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">Hi Martin,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">  </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">As a workaround, you can just add a layer which takes fill as a valid aesthetic (I guess, after looking at the online documentation, that’s the reason why if you only include geom_crossbar the fill doesn’t appear in the legend [e.g. hollow bar …]); in the code bellow I just added geom_smooth() (you only receive a warning saying you have only one x value and nothing to draw). </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">  </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">Hope this helps, and congratulations,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">fernando</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">  </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">  </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">ggplot(df, aes(fill = group, colour = group, y = resp, x = trt)) +</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                geom_crossbar(limits,  width = 0.7, position = position_dodge(width = 0.8), size = 0.8) +</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                geom_smooth() +</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                scale_fill_manual(values = alpha(c(&quot;white&quot;, &quot;black&quot;), 0.3), name = &quot;&quot;) +</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                scale_colour_manual(values = c(&quot;black&quot;, &quot;black&quot;), name = &quot;&quot;) +</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                scale_y_continuous(breaks = seq(36, 50, 2), name = &quot;&quot;) +</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                scale_x_discrete(name = &quot;&quot;) +</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                opts(legend.position =\n c(0.764, 0.833),</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                               legend.background = theme_rect(colour = 0),</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                               legend.text = theme_text(face = &quot;italic&quot;, size = 20),</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                               legend.title = theme_blank()) +</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                opts(axis.text.x = theme_text(size = 20, vjust = 1),</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                               axis.text.y = theme_text(size = 20, hjust = 1)) +</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                opts(axis.title.x = theme_text(size = 27, hjust = 0.561, vjust = 0.3),</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                               axis.title.y = theme_text(size = 27, angle = 90, vjust = 0.685, hjust = 0.78)) +</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">                opts(plot.margin = unit (c(1.1, 1, 1.28, 1.23), &quot;lines&quot;))</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" name=\"m_271634395666330372__MailEndCompose\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">  </span></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:rgb(31,73,125)\" lang=\"EN-US\">  </span></p><div><div style=\"border-width:1pt medium medium;border-style:solid none none;border-color:rgb(181,196,223) -moz-use-text-color -moz-use-text-color;padding:3pt 0cm 0cm\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;\" lang=\"ES\">De:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;sans-serif&quot;\" lang=\"ES\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>] <b>En nombre de </b>Martin Kärcher<br><b>Enviado el:</b> jueves, 25 de noviembre de 2010 18:57<br><b>Para:</b> ggplot2<br><b>Asunto:</b> fill in legend of black &amp; white crossbar plot</span></p></div></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">\n  </p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Dear all,</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\">I have prepared a coloured graph (attached) for publication in a journal which I now have to change into black and white </span><span style=\"font-family:Wingdings;color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\">:-(</span><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> (attached). Otherwise, I’d have to pay ca. 1000 $ for 3 graphs, seriously.</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\">I have attached a reproducible R script. It first presents the graph in\n colour and then in black and white which shows the dilemma.</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Ideally, I would like to have the “line” AND the “fill” in the legend, not only the “line”. “Fill” only would be good too. Of course I could use different line types but for a crossbar it would look a bit stupid. The other alternative would be to use a white line for the second group but really, that would not produce a great legend as well.</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\">If anybody could help me include the fill in the legend or has a good\n alternative I would be very grateful.</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Best wishes,</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\">Martin</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\">p.s.: The session info is:</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"># R version 2.12.0 (2010-10-15)</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"># Platform: i386-pc-mingw32/i386 (32-bit)</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"># locale:</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"># [1] LC_COLLATE=German_Austria.1252  LC_CTYPE=German_Austria.1252    LC_MONETARY=German_Austria.1252 LC_NUMERIC=C                    LC_TIME=German_Austria.1252    </span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span><span sty